From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:41:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Size the PMGR wake-time block
 to the words read

The pmgr_sleep "wake-time" region covered the whole page at 0x380760000.
apple-sleep requests it with devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(),
and the GPU TVM power controller (gfx_tvm, 0x380760800) lies in the same
page, so on the J604 apple-gfx-tvm failed to claim its register with
-EBUSY, its power domain never came up and the GPU stayed in deferred
probe: no AGX, Hyprland not on the GPU (1.609 W6 boot, /proc/iomem
"380760000-380760fff : 3882c8000.power-management wake-time").

apple-sleep only reads the counter control word at 0x0 and the T8132
wake-time counter slots 64 and 66 (config at 0x100 + 16 * idx, value at
+8/+0xc), so the last word it touches is 0x52c. Size the region to
0x530, which ends below the TVM controller, and say why in the comment.

Fixes: dd97a1f960 ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Describe the system sleep controls")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi
index 1c315a4afb..0dacfb1417 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi
@@ -34,7 +34,10 @@
 	/*
 	 * PMGR sleep-state counters, AP wake sources and sleep exit times. ADT
 	 * PMGR ranges: event counters 0x3882c8000 (PMGR_AON + 0x48000), wake
-	 * 0x388004000, wake-time 0x380760000 (PMGR + 0x60000). Offsets inside
+	 * 0x388004000, wake-time 0x380760000 (PMGR + 0x60000), sized to the words
+	 * apple-sleep
+	 * reads (CTL at 0x0, counter slots 64 and 66 up to 0x52f): the GPU
+	 * TVM power controller sits at 0x380760800 in the same page. Offsets inside
 	 * each block are the T6020 ones: TO-VERIFY (bring-up kit reads
 	 * /sys/kernel/debug/apple-sleep/regs first). No CPM range: the T6020
 	 * CPM gating words (PMGR + 0xc030..) are not known on T8132, and a
@@ -44,7 +47,7 @@
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmgr-sleep";
 		reg = <0x3 0x882c8000 0x0 0x1000>,
 		      <0x3 0x88004000 0x0 0x60>,
-		      <0x3 0x80760000 0x0 0x1000>;
+		      <0x3 0x80760000 0x0 0x530>;
 		reg-names = "events", "wake", "wake-time";
 		/*
 		 * The J604 ADT "ap-wake-sources" list, unchanged: AOP CPU wakeup,
